@[spell-caches step]
Select the spell caches (built packages) on the ISO that you want installed on
top of the basesystem; they are in /var/cache/sorcery/. You need at least
@[grub2] (boot loader, BIOS and UEFI); on UEFI machines also @[efibootmgr] and
@[dosfstools]; plus the tools for your filesystems (@[xfsprogs],
@[btrfs-progs]) and anything else you like (e.g. @[openssh], or @[vim] and
@[jed] next to the base system's nano). Dependencies they need are added
automatically when they are installed.

  @[enchantment select caches]              # menu: space toggles, enter accepts
  @[enchantment select caches show]         # list the selection
  @[enchantment select caches add 'grub2*'] # add files matching a pattern
  @[enchantment select caches del 'grub2*'] # remove files matching a pattern
  @[enchantment select caches all]         # (or none) all or nothing

The selection is a plain list of file names, one per line, which you can also
edit directly: @[$EDITOR $ENCHANT_TMP/spell-caches]

You can change it at any time until you install the caches in the basesystem
step. When you are finished selecting, type @[next].
